        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(linux-node): preserve emoji in command failure details",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Linux node notification, camera, or location failures could return malformed Unicode when command output placed an emoji or another supplementary character across the diagnostic length limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe existing Plugin SDK UTF-16-safe truncation helper now applies after whitespace normalization while preserving the existing 300-code-unit limit and error selection behavior. A focused regression test covers both the formatted detail and the resulting tool error.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLinux node command failures now return well-formed error text. Commands whose diagnostics do not cross the truncation boundary are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- AI-assisted: yes. The implementation and affected call paths were reviewed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/linux-node/src/command-utils.test.ts` - 1/1 test passed.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` - passed.\n- Focused validation used the local fallback because Blacksmith Testbox was unavailable and sanitized AWS Crabbox could not acquire a lease.\n- Initial CI run [29359479449](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29359479449) completed. Selected build, type, contract, QA smoke, and test lanes passed. The three failing source checks reproduce only current-base debt outside this PR: an unused Bonjour export, a stale QA Lab max-lines baseline entry, and two over-limit system-agent files.\n",
